Article 42

(1) Special Protection for Children Exploited Economically and/or Sexually as referred to in Article 38 paragraph (2) letter d, is implemented through:

a. dissemination and/or socialization of provisions of laws and regulations related to the protection of Children Exploited Economically and/or Sexually;
b. monitoring, reporting, and imposition of sanctions; and c. involvement of various companies, labor unions, non-governmental organizations, and the community in the elimination of economic and/or sexual exploitation of children.
(2) In the case that Children Exploited Economically and/or sexually require restoration of conditions to their original state, services must be provided in the form of:
a. medical rehabilitation;
b. social rehabilitation;
c. legal assistance and social assistance; and/or d. repatriation and social reintegration.

