Article 55

In order to achieve the objectives of protecting women (1) and children victims of violence, the Regional Government may cooperate with:

a. the central government;
b. the provincial government;
c. other regency/city governments;
d. law enforcement institutions/ and/or law enforcement officers;
e. non-governmental organizations;
f. the community;
g. universities/ academics; and
h. mass media.

Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: (2)

a. exchange of data and information;

b. recovery of victims of violence;

c. repatriation and social reintegration;

d. provision of evidence and witnesses; and

e. followed up in accordance with applicable law. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (3)

(2) is set forth in the form of a cooperation agreement in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
